{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449537-the-syndicate-hardest-to-corrupt-from-outside-easiest-to-fall-on-their-own","id":1449537,"title":"The Syndicate: Hardest to corrupt from outside, easiest to fall on their own","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-25T04:33:39-07:00","id":1449537,"title":"The Syndicate: Hardest to corrupt from outside, easiest to fall on their own","content":"Hello Everyone,<br /> <br /> Some time ago I was talking with a friend about the technocratic convention that everyone loves to hate, the Syndicate. The common perception is that they are a bunch of amoral greedy sociopaths that will step on anything and everyone that gets in their way, and because of this they are the main reason for the corruption within the Union. It's a generalization of course, but one more accurate that anyone within the convention would like to admit. In any case, I was arguing how that makes them prime targets for corruption from the nephandi and my pal told me it was the opposite. That's when he said that they were they are hardest to corrupt from the outside but had the easiest time falling on their own.<br /> <br /> His argument goes like this, it's important to remember that the Syndicate are the masters of the ars cupidae or art of desire, nobody understands better what people want and how to use that to manipulate them. So, when a nephandi comes along playing the game of temptation most Syndicate operatives would raise an eyebrow amused and play them back. Sure, some syndicate operatives will bite more than they can chew but hey, \u00bfThat's the game right? No risk no fun, being a Syndicate &quot;Mage&quot; is all about dancing at the edge of the abyss to get everything you want without falling to reckless ambition and greed. It is this perspective more than anything that allows them to identify what Nephandi are doing, because it is in many ways the same perspective of the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> That said, few have the discipline and cunning to navigate the edge without falling. That's why my pal also argued that the greatest danger to the convention are themselves. When you're good at playing the game of the art of desire you start to believe that you can get whatever you want (and it's worse if it's actually true), this quickly evolves in believing you deserve everything you want. From there hubris takes over, and it's only a few steps into infernalism or worse. Because of this, I'm sure that some Nephandi would argue that the easiest way to corrupt the Syndicate is to just leave them be. <br /> <br /> So with all this said I'm curious to know your opinion \u00bfDo you think that the Syndicate's culture makes them harder to corrupt from the outside? <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your answers. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T05:20:26-07:00","id":1449542,"title":"","content":"I think corrupting members of the Syndicate is abit like going up to a member of Ix and asking &quot;hey do you want some cyberware?&quot; Are there IXers who's Paradigm isn't &quot;The Flesh is weak&quot; probably but they aren't super common. Are there Syndicate members who's Paradigm isn't &quot;Everything is for sale, everything can be bought&quot; but its a pretty common one and definately what the perspective character of Syndicate REvised clearly holds as true. Its also how you get Primal Utility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T06:56:20-07:00","id":1449550,"title":"","content":"I was toying with this during a Technocracy chronicle I planned to start but never got past the first introductory story, wherein I planned for the Syndicate PC's individual story to introduce the first major chronicle-wide plot hook. Long story short, it was Pizzagate before Pizzagate was even a thing, except run by Nephandi who had infiltrated the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> The key that's being missed, is who would give a shit about corrupting Syndicate agents? It's likely better for most Nephandi to stay largely hands-off on matters internal to the Syndicate, to minimize their footprint on the convention and avoid scrutiny. The Syndicate's already the near-perfect front organization for most shit Nephandi might do, why would they go and do something stupid like try to fix what isn't broken?<br /> <br /> But in the broader sense, the Syndicate's the one convention people can't really examine impartially. Contrast them against, say, the Progenitors whom it seems everyone wants to love (after all, they just want the masses to live longer, healthier lives, right?), when that same &quot;everyone&quot; is incredibly quick to compartmentalize and dismiss the unadulterated harm and evil Progenitors have committed like every other convention. The Syndicate is (superficially) too interwoven with and dependent upon capitalism to judge on its own merits, meaning one's opinion of capitalism is going to have an undeniable, unavoidable, effect on their opinion of the Syndicate. That's not really fertile ground for consistent, reliable answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T07:57:07-07:00","id":1449554,"title":"","content":"Right. Keep in mind that the NWO are the masters of Dominion, which is fundamentally about subverting free will. That gives them a sense of power and entitlement that's every bit as corrupting as what Tte Syndicate gets from the Art of Desire. And their knowledge of psychology should supposedly give them the same kind of protection against Nephandic infiltration that the Syndicate supposedly has. <br /> <br /> As Theodrim says, getting an objective answer to where the rot in the Technocracy lies is challenging. If you view capitalism as evil and in need of being reined in by a powerful government, then you're going to sympathize with the NWO and view the Syndicate as the root of all evil. If you have a more libertarian bent, your view is more likely to be the opposite: sure, some regulation of the economy is needed to curb the worst of the abuses; but give too much power to the government, and it will turn you into a de facto slave. And with no accountability, corruption in the government (or in this case, in the NWO) will run rampant. As such, while there are problems in the Syndicate, the heart of the rot in the Technocracy lies in the NWO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-25-2021, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T08:43:34-07:00","id":1449557,"title":"","content":"My question wasn't about where the root of the corruption within the technocracy lies (I blame the leadership of all the conventions, with the Syndicate and the NWO being the worst offenders in their own way), but you make some interesting points.<br /> Now, I didn't mention the NWO and their mastery of psychodynamics because I make the distinction, (perhaps wrongly), about knowing the human mind and knowing desire. Sure, they're both related, but to make it clearer, I consider them separate specialities within the same field. There's no question that the NWO are masters of the human mind, but it's the Syndicate who knows the human heart.<br /> When I think about nephandi, I picture them as the archetypical tempter or snake in the garden if you will, dangling the fruit of knowledge in front of your face and convincing you why it is a good idea to take it. In this scenario, the NWO would be a wise nature man who knows what the snake is and why it's so dangerous, \u00bfThe Syndicate? They understand the snake because they are snakes themselves. That's why I believe that it's harder for the Syndicate to get fooled by tactics that, quite frankly, they know like the back of their hand. <br /> \u00bfDoes this make them harder to fool by Nephandi? Perhaps, then again the Nephandi may have developed new tactics with the Syndicate in mind or like it was mentioned perhaps they know they just have to wait to let unchecked greed and ambition do the job. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T09:40:46-07:00","id":1449562,"title":"","content":"Despite the name, the Art of Desire is not about \u201call things related to the heart\u201d. It zeros in on one specific drive, desire; and it does so in the context of valuation: determining how much something is worth to someone. That is, it is fundamentally about what we today call economics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T09:57:55-07:00","id":1449563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449537-the-syndicate-hardest-to-corrupt-from-outside-easiest-to-fall-on-their-own?p=1449554#post1449554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...As such, while there are problems in the Syndicate, the heart of the rot in the Technocracy lies in the NWO.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say any individual convention bears the greatest responsibility for the Technocracy's state is in grave error, in my opinion. They're all equally liable for their own part in it -- even the Void Engineers -- in my opinion.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm keeping my commentary to the Syndicate since this is a Syndicate thread.<br /> <br /> The bias raises itself explicitly even in how the Syndicate is characterized. &quot;Everything can be bought, everything can be sold&quot; is a fair maxim for a Syndicate paradigm, sure. But what about &quot;the rising tide lifts all boats&quot;, or dare we suggest, &quot;from each according to their ability, to each according to their need&quot;?<br /> <br /> And yes, I am absolutely, positively suggesting not just the existence, but viability, of Communist Syndicate agents. Note that I said the Syndicate is <i>superficially</i> interwoven and dependent upon capitalism.<br /> <br /> Here's the rub: we get tied up and bogged down discussing capitol, value, and trade in terms of goods and services. That only encapsulates two, perhaps, three forms of capitol: financial, material, and living. What of social, intellectual, experiential, spiritual, and cultural capitol? It's only natural we get bogged down here, because we live in an economy of scarcity of natural and human resources, which places undue value and priority upon the three most basic, rudimentary, and immediate forms of capitol, and the latter five are only experienced and valued in the context of the former three's acquisition and preservation.<br /> <br /> A post-scarcity economy wouldn't be the end of capitol: it would be the <i>beginning</i> of it. Because those other five forms of capitol would at last be equal, and exchange of those forms would be acknowledged, free, and ideal in a post-scarcity society. That's why Primal Utility is so great; it's a grand unified theory of value, unlinked from any individual form of capitol. That <i>is</i> the Syndicate view of Ascension, what differs is which economic theories are likely to get humanity there.<br /> <br /> The other four conventions are groups of mages whose lofty aspirations for all humankind are limited by the methodologies and consensuses of their time, and not least the egos of those who practice those shared paradigms and are afraid to loosen their grasp on power for the sake of long-term gain. Syndicate's no different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T10:26:03-07:00","id":1449565,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> : just to be clear, I wasn't saying that the NWO really does bear all of the guilt. I was pointing out how a difference view on politics and economics can lead to an opposite conclusion. That said, I can see how what I wrote could be taken as me claiming it to be an objective fact. Thus, this clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T10:27:23-07:00","id":1449566,"title":"","content":"The idea of a Communist Syndicate isn't that surprising. The technocracy has had a hand in most of the major social, political, and economic fashions that have popped up over the years. Not necessarily as inventors, but certainly as strong advocates. In my head canon the Syndicate had to be invested in Communism and I don't think they've dropped it either, though it is clearly not their main focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T10:45:45-07:00","id":1449567,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, that's a result of The Syndicate being the only faction in the game that focuses primarily on economics. Or at least it was until Book of the Fallen introduced the Mammonites, which I read as \u201cwhat happens when a Syndic Falls\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-25T11:16:46-07:00","id":1449569,"title":"","content":"For me it is less that they are the only economics focused faction and more that they are an economics focused Technocracy faction. It's actually hard for me to consider them not experimenting with multiple economic theories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T03:10:45-07:00","id":1449637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1449537-the-syndicate-hardest-to-corrupt-from-outside-easiest-to-fall-on-their-own?p=1449569#post1449569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it is less that they are the only economics focused faction and more that they are an economics focused Technocracy faction. It's actually hard for me to consider them not experimenting with multiple economic theories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And yet that's not what Syndicate revised says...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}